WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
In this example, total capacity is 64 thousand tokens.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.900
We reserve 8 thousand for output, 4 thousand for margin and 4 thousand for mandatory instructions.

3
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:22.250
That leaves 48 thousand for dynamic information. This is not a universal model property.

4
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:31.050
A 42-thousand-token log crowds out necessary files within a 48-thousand-token budget.

5
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:37.900
We extract relevant failures and keep a reference to the complete log.

6
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:45.950
The contract and files now fit. The extraction must retain the error that matters.

7
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:53.300
The source says: return within fourteen days, except opened items.

8
00:00:53.300 --> 00:01:00.850
A summary keeps the deadline but drops the exception. It looks correct but changes the decision.

9
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:08.200
The compaction check tests both conditions and rejects this loss.

10
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:15.550
Summary S derives from document revision A through a lossy transformation.

11
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:22.400
When the revision changes, S is no longer validated for the current state.

12
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:29.750
Provenance lets us recover the affected passage without regenerating everything by default.

13
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:37.417
Reusing a cached prefix avoids repeated processing work, subject to the provider contract.

14
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:44.583
The content remains part of the logical input. Nothing has been selected or summarised.

15
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:51.933
Compaction replaces the earlier representation. That transformation can lose information.

16
00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:59.283
The context stores a short ID for file A rather than every line.

17
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:06.450
When detail is needed, the read requests revision A and verifies its identity.

18
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:15.250
If only B is returned, it is not presented as A. Saving context creates a recovery obligation.

